{
  "_comment": "Vault OS global settings template, matching the owner's working settings minus personal values. installer/install-claude-layer.py backs up ~/.claude/settings.json, then adds only what is missing: top-level keys, and entry by entry the maps enabledPlugins, extraKnownMarketplaces, skillOverrides, modelSettings and env; the hooks come from hooks/hooks.json (filtered per platform). Existing user values always win. No tokens, no personal paths. permissions stays in the safe default mode; --bypass-permissions (asked in the quiz) adds the owner's bypass mode and allow list. Plugins set to false are optional: enable them in /plugin when you need them. skillOverrides decide which skills are off, listed by name only, or reachable only when typed (user-invocable-only).",
